    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Notebook 02 — Final RibFrac 500-Patient Preprocessing and Patient Registry\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook is the **final preprocessing/registry stage** for the RibFrac labelled development cohort.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Source cohort\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Training Part 1: 300 CTs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Training Part 2: 120 CTs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Tuning/Validation: 80 CTs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Total labelled patients: **500**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Final patient-level protocol\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The three labelled sources are combined first and then split at the **patient level**:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Training: 350 patients\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Validation: 75 patients\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Internal test: 75 patients\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The internal test set is distinct from the official RibFrac challenge test set, whose ground truth is not publicly available.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Important storage design\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The full 1-mm isotropic preprocessed volumes are **not permanently materialized for all 500 patients** in `/kaggle/working`. Instead, this notebook:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. validates all source metadata;\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. creates and saves the final patient registry/split;\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. provides a reproducible, on-demand patient preprocessing function;\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. optionally materializes selected patients for smoke testing.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Notebook 03 can use the same on-demand preprocessing logic to extract patches patient-by-patient, avoiding a 100+ GB intermediate volume store.\\n\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"id\": \"f998bd3c876879aa\"\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Cell 1 — Imports\\n\",\n",
